# Multi-bit gates for quantum computing

Xiaoguang Wang, Anders Sørensen, and Klaus Mølmer

Institute of Physics and Astronomy, University of Aarhus, DK-8000 Århus C, Denmark

arXiv:quant-ph/0012055v2 (14 Mar 2001); published as Phys. Rev. A **64**, 062309 (2001).

## Abstract

We present a general technique to implement products of many qubit operators
communicating via a joint harmonic oscillator degree of freedom in a quantum
computer. By conditional displacements and rotations we can implement
Hamiltonians which are trigonometric functions of qubit operators. With such
operators we can effectively implement higher order gates such as Toffoli gates
and $C^n$-NOT gates, and we show that the entire Grover search algorithm can be
implemented in a direct way.

## Core identity (Eq. 1)

$$
e^{i\lambda_1 x \hat A}\, e^{i\lambda_2 p \hat B}\, e^{-i\lambda_1 x \hat A}\,
e^{-i\lambda_2 p \hat B}
\;=\; e^{-i\lambda_1\lambda_2 \hat A\hat B},
\qquad [\hat A,\hat B]=0.
\tag{1}
$$

## Generalized Hamiltonian (Eq. 2) and propagator (Eq. 3)

$$
H(t) \;=\; v(t)\hat A\, x \;+\; w(t)\hat B\, p \;+\; r(t)\hat C\, n .
\tag{2}
$$

$$
U(t) \;=\; e^{-i\hat S(t)}\, e^{-i n \hat R(t)}\,
e^{-i x \hat V(t)}\, e^{-i p \hat W(t)} .
\tag{3}
$$

with
$$
\hat R(t) \;=\; \hat C \int_0^t r(t')\,dt',
$$
$$
\hat V(t) \;=\; \int_0^t \!\!\bigl[\hat A\, v(t')\cos\hat R(t') - \hat B\, w(t')\sin\hat R(t')\bigr]\,dt',
$$
$$
\hat W(t) \;=\; \int_0^t \!\!\bigl[\hat B\, w(t')\cos\hat R(t') + \hat A\, v(t')\sin\hat R(t')\bigr]\,dt',
$$
$$
\hat S(t) \;=\; -\int_0^t \hat V(t')\bigl[\hat B\, w(t')\cos\hat R(t') + \hat A\, v(t')\sin\hat R(t')\bigr]\,dt'.
\tag{4}
$$

## Toffoli Hamiltonian (Eq. 5) — the central testable claim

$$
H \;=\; \Omega\!\left[
\frac{\sigma_z^{(1)}+\sigma_z^{(2)}+1}{4\sqrt{K}}\,x
\;-\; \sigma_x^{(3)}\!\left(n + \frac{1}{32K}\right)
\right].
\tag{5}
$$

Turning $H$ on for $\tau = K\cdot 2\pi/\Omega$ yields
$$
U(\tau) \;=\; \exp\!\left(-i\pi\,\frac{(\sigma_z^{(1)}+1)(\sigma_z^{(2)}+1)\,\sigma_x^{(3)}}{8}\right),
$$
which is the C$^2$-NOT (Toffoli) gate up to a global phase, independent of the
oscillator's initial state.

## Fourier identity for $C^{n_c}$-NOT (Eq. 6)

$$
\prod_{l=1}^{n_c} \frac{\sigma_z^{(l)}+1}{2}
\;=\; \frac{1}{n_c+1}\sum_{k=1}^{n_c+1}
\cos\!\left(\frac{2\pi k}{n_c+1}\,(\hat J_z - J)\right),
\qquad \hat J_z = \sum_{l=1}^{n_c}\!\!\frac{\sigma_z^{(l)}-1}{2}.
\tag{6}
$$

## Grover mean-inversion (Eq. 8-10)

$$
U_G \;=\; \frac{2}{N}M - I \;=\; \exp\!\Bigl(i\pi\, \prod_{l=0}^{n-1}\!\tfrac{\sigma_x^{(l)}+1}{2}\Bigr).
\tag{10}
$$

$$
U_f \;=\; \exp\!\Bigl(i\pi\, \prod_{l=0}^{n-1}\!\tfrac{\sigma_z^{(l)}+2 b_l - 1}{2}\Bigr).
\tag{7}
$$
